  "Question": "What is the value of\n\n\\[ \\begin{aligned} &(1 + 11 + 21 + 31 + 41) \\\\ &\\quad {}+ (9 + 19 + 29 + 39 + 49)? \\end{aligned} \\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(150\\)",
    "B": "\\(199\\)",
    "C": "\\(200\\)",
    "D": "\\(249\\)",
    "E": "\\(250\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Pair the smallest addend with the largest, then continue inward. This makes five equal sums:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n&(1+49)+(11+39)+(21+29)\\\\\n&\\quad +(31+19)+(41+9)\\\\\n&=5\\cdot50=250.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nEvery original addend appears exactly once, so reordering and grouping preserve the sum. The value is \\(250\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{E}\\).",
